WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:10.538
This is the ANC Presentations dashboard. Every deck you own is listed here, with its tracking links, client activity, and engagement analytics one click away.

00:11.338 --> 00:22.074
Open a deck in the builder. Once the story is in order and saved, the Share button at the top is how the client receives it. A client never gets the file, only a link that you control.

00:22.874 --> 00:34.394
Share checks the deck before anything goes out. If template text or another client's name is still on a page, it tells you the exact slide and stops. Fix the page, then come back.

00:35.194 --> 00:45.068
When the deck is clean, give the link a name, for example who it is for. Switch on Ask viewers for name and email when you want to know exactly who opened it.

00:45.868 --> 00:57.937
Go live, create link and copy publishes the deck, creates the tracked link, and puts it on your clipboard. Every link you create appears in the list with its own analytics, and any link can be revoked at any time.

00:58.737 --> 01:12.765
Before you send, open Preflight from the More menu and run it. Ready to send means the published version, the client link, the media, the desktop and phone rendering, the PDF, and the client-ready content have all been proven.

01:13.965 --> 01:23.055
This is what the client sees when the link asks for identity. They enter their name, work email, and company once, and the deck opens.

01:23.855 --> 01:35.192
The client moves through the presentation in the browser. Every page they reach and how long they stay is recorded against their link, and the decision bar lets them approve, ask a question, or request a revision.

01:35.992 --> 01:50.020
Back on your side, the analytics page shows who opened the deck, how far they got, where they dropped off, the device they used, and any decision they took. Export the same data as a spreadsheet from the dashboard row whenever you need it.
